INT. NIGHT FERRY - GALLEY - NIGHT

A cramped steel galley below the car deck. Condensation drips from pipes. A coffee urn gurgles. Six crew crowd a bolted table beneath a swinging lamp. The engine drones through the floor.

CAPTAIN EZEKIEL FARROW, 60s, at the head, stirs a mug he doesn't drink. FIRST MATE ODESSA LIN, 40s, flips through a logbook. COOK BARNABY OKORO, 50s, wipes a spotless counter. DECKHAND SVEN HALLGREN, 20s, jiggles his knee. NAVIGATOR PRIYANKA DESHMUKH, 30s, studies a chart. And at the end, ENGINEER YURI KOZLOV, 50s, an oil-stained cap in his fist.

CAPTAIN FARROW
(to the table)
I called you here because someone has been in the cargo hold.

LIN
Which hold?

CAPTAIN FARROW
The sealed one.

SVEN
There's no sealed hold.

CAPTAIN FARROW
There is now.

BARNABY
(muttering)
I never liked this run.

PRIYANKA
Captain, the manifest lists nothing sealed.

CAPTAIN FARROW
The manifest was edited.

LIN
By whom?

CAPTAIN FARROW
By someone with access.

YURI
That's all of us.

CAPTAIN FARROW
Yes. That's the point.

A heavy silence. The lamp swings. Sven stops jiggling his knee.

SVEN
Is it dangerous?

CAPTAIN FARROW
I don't know.

BARNABY
Then why tell us?

CAPTAIN FARROW
Because one of you already knows.

Nobody moves. Priyanka sets down her pen. Lin closes the logbook.

LIN
(to the Captain)
You think it's one of us.

CAPTAIN FARROW
I think it is two of you.

YURI
Then say who.

CAPTAIN FARROW
I will not. Not yet.

SVEN
(under his breath)
This is insane.

PRIYANKA
(to Sven)
Sit still.

SVEN
I am sitting.

PRIYANKA
You are vibrating.

BARNABY
(to himself)
Thirty years at sea and I'm cooking for a hanging.

CAPTAIN FARROW
(to the whole table, calmly)
At the next port, a team boards. Customs, perhaps police. Anyone wishing to speak before then, my door is open.

LIN
And if no one does?

CAPTAIN FARROW
Then I will have to guess.

The lamp swings. The engine drones. A faint knocking begins, somewhere far below the floor, slow and patient, like a fist on a locked door. Every head turns.
